00:23:28.640 --> 00:23:30.575
RELY ON GASOLINE TO DROP THEIR

00:23:30.642 --> 00:23:32.444
CHILDREN OFF FOR SCHOOL OR TO GO

00:23:32.511 --> 00:23:34.045
TO WORK EVERY SINGLE DAY. THE

00:23:34.112 --> 00:23:35.280
FACT THAT THE STORAGE

00:23:35.347 --> 00:23:36.248
REQUIREMENT DECREASES PRICES IS

00:23:36.314 --> 00:23:39.785
AT MY CONCLUSION OR BIG OIL'S

00:23:39.851 --> 00:23:41.787
CONCLUSION. IT'S WHAT THE STAFF

00:23:41.853 --> 00:23:42.888
AT THE ENERGY COMMISSION

00:23:42.954 --> 00:23:44.623
BELIEVES WILL HAPPEN. THERE IS

00:23:44.689 --> 00:23:46.458
ALSO A LIKELY SCENARIO THAT

00:23:46.525 --> 00:23:47.459
GASOLINE SHORTAGES WILL TAKE

00:23:47.526 --> 00:23:49.995
EFFECT BECAUSE OF THE MILLION

00:23:50.061 --> 00:23:51.196
DOLLAR A DAY PENALTY THAT COULD

00:23:51.263 --> 00:23:52.497
POTENTIALLY BE CHARGED TO

00:23:52.564 --> 00:23:54.466
REFINERS, AND THAT WOULD BE ON A

00:23:54.533 --> 00:23:55.700
DOWNSTREAM SITUATION, WHICH I'LL

00:23:55.767 --> 00:23:56.668
EXPLAIN. WHILE THE

00:23:56.735 --> 00:23:59.037
ADMINISTRATION CLAIMS THAT THE

00:23:59.104 --> 00:24:00.172
INCREASED STORAGE WILL HAVE SAVE

00:24:00.238 --> 00:24:02.174
CONSUMERS MONEY BY SMOOTHING OUT

00:24:02.240 --> 00:24:03.875
GAS SPIKES, THERE'S NO EVIDENCE

00:24:03.942 --> 00:24:05.877
TO SUPPORT THAT THEORY. AND IT

00:24:05.944 --> 00:24:07.512
CERTAINLY DIDN'T FACTOR IN THE

00:24:07.579 --> 00:24:08.780
INCREASED COST ASSOCIATED WITH

00:24:08.847 --> 00:24:10.448
THE ADDITIONAL STORAGE AND

00:24:10.515 --> 00:24:11.016
DOWNSTREAM SUPPLY SHORTAGES.

00:24:11.082 --> 00:24:13.552
LIKE MOST OF THE THINGS DONE IN

00:24:13.618 --> 00:24:14.553
HEAVY REGULATORY HAND OF

00:24:14.619 --> 00:24:17.322
GOVERNMENT, THIS IS BOUND TO

00:24:17.389 --> 00:24:18.456
INCREASE THE PRICE OF GASOLINE

00:24:18.523 --> 00:24:20.091
INSTEAD OF LOWER IT. IT'S EASY

00:24:20.158 --> 00:24:21.193
TO MAKE THE ARGUMENT THAT

00:24:21.259 --> 00:24:23.295
CALIFORNIA HAS THE HIGHEST COST

00:24:23.361 --> 00:24:25.397
OF GASOLINE FOR THIS VERY

00:24:25.463 --> 00:24:26.498
REASON. THE LOW CARBON FUEL

00:24:26.565 --> 00:24:28.500
STANDARDS AB FIVE, WHICH

00:24:28.567 --> 00:24:29.534
RESTRICTED OUR TRUCKING AND

00:24:29.601 --> 00:24:31.469
TRANSPORTATION AND INCREASED THE

00:24:31.536 --> 00:24:32.470
COST OF TRUCKING AND

00:24:32.537 --> 00:24:33.405
TRANSPORTATION REQUIREMENTS, OUR

00:24:33.471 --> 00:24:35.040
SPECIAL BLEND AND MANY OF THESE

00:24:35.106 --> 00:24:36.875
OTHERS REGULATORY PROCESSES HAVE

00:24:36.942 --> 00:24:39.344
DRIVEN UP THE COST OF

00:24:39.411 --> 00:24:42.113
CALIFORNIA'S FUEL, MAKING IT THE

00:24:42.180 --> 00:24:43.281
HIGHEST IN THE NATION. THERE'S A

00:24:43.348 --> 00:24:45.550
HANDFUL OF MAJOR REFINERIES THAT

00:24:45.617 --> 00:24:47.352
ARE STILL LEFT HERE IN THE STATE

00:24:47.419 --> 00:24:49.621
OF CALIFORNIA 50 YEARS AGO. WE

00:24:49.688 --> 00:24:51.289
HAVE TO. WE USED TO HAVE 50 THAT

00:24:51.356 --> 00:24:54.426
WE USED TO HAVE A DOZEN MORE

00:24:54.492 --> 00:24:55.493
REFINERIES 50 YEARS AGO, AND

00:24:55.560 --> 00:24:57.062
WE'VE LOST THEM IN THE LAST 50

00:24:57.128 --> 00:24:59.064
YEARS. A HANDFUL OF MAJOR

00:24:59.130 --> 00:25:00.232
REFINERIES ARE LEFT. AND TO SHUT

00:25:00.298 --> 00:25:03.268
DOWN THE RIPPLE, IF JUST A FEW

00:25:03.335 --> 00:25:04.469
SHUT DOWN, THE RIPPLE EFFECTS

00:25:04.536 --> 00:25:05.537
WOULD BE CATASTROPHIC TO OUR

00:25:05.604 --> 00:25:06.905
CONSUMERS. OUR REFINERIES ALSO

00:25:06.972 --> 00:25:08.006
PROVIDE ABOUT 90% OF NEVADA'S

00:25:08.073 --> 00:25:12.677
FUEL AND ALSO 50% OF ARIZONA'S

00:25:12.744 --> 00:25:13.945
FUEL. SO I DO HAVE A QUESTION

00:25:14.012 --> 00:25:16.815
THAT I THINK ALL OF US NEED TO

00:25:16.882 --> 00:25:17.983
ANSWER IN THE MEDIA SHOULD

00:25:18.049 --> 00:25:19.818
PROBABLY PRESS EVERY LEGISLATOR

00:25:19.885 --> 00:25:21.253
WHO VOTES FOR THIS BILL ON THIS

00:25:21.319 --> 00:25:22.320
QUESTION. WE HAVE THE SAME

00:25:22.387 --> 00:25:24.322
SUPPLY CHAIN. CALIFORNIA DOESN'T

00:25:24.389 --> 00:25:26.057
GET A DIFFERENT SUPPLY CHAIN FOR

00:25:26.124 --> 00:25:27.893
ITS CRUDE OIL THAN IT DOES IF IT

00:25:27.959 --> 00:25:29.728
SUPPLIES IT TO CALIFORNIA,

00:25:29.794 --> 00:25:31.830
ARIZONA OR NEVADA. SO WE HAVE A

00:25:31.897 --> 00:25:33.064
DIFFERENT WE HAVE THE SAME

00:25:33.131 --> 00:25:34.165
SUPPLY CHAIN. WE GET IT FROM

00:25:34.232 --> 00:25:35.300
FOREIGN COUNTRIES. IT COMES

00:25:35.367 --> 00:25:36.501
ACROSS OUR ECOSYSTEM. WE'VE

00:25:36.568 --> 00:25:38.203
TALKED ABOUT THAT SEVERAL TIMES.

00:25:38.270 --> 00:25:40.272
WE DON'T PRODUCE IT HERE IN

00:25:40.338 --> 00:25:41.339
CALIFORNIA ANYMORE. WE CAN'T GET

00:25:41.406 --> 00:25:42.240
