00:26:03.862 --> 00:26:05.363
IT INTO TRUCKS. SOME PIPELINE

00:26:05.430 --> 00:26:06.398
AND RAIL CAR, BUT MOSTLY

00:26:06.464 --> 00:26:08.133
TRUCKING AND TRANSPORTATION. AND

00:26:08.199 --> 00:26:10.335
THEY PROVIDE THAT TO OUR

00:26:10.402 --> 00:26:12.470
RETAILERS OR OUR DOWNSTREAM

00:26:12.537 --> 00:26:13.571
FACILITIES, WHICH ARE THE GAS

00:26:13.638 --> 00:26:15.974
STATIONS THAT ALL OF OUR

00:26:16.041 --> 00:26:17.042
CONSUMERS USE EVERY SINGLE DAY

00:26:17.108 --> 00:26:19.044
TO PUT FUEL IN THEIR CAR. THOSE

00:26:19.110 --> 00:26:22.480
SAME TRUCKS, THAT SAME PROCESS,

00:26:22.547 --> 00:26:23.581
THE SAME POINT OF ORIGIN, THE

00:26:23.648 --> 00:26:26.117
SAME POINT OF ORIGIN, WHICH THE

00:26:26.184 --> 00:26:27.953
PRODUCT ORIGINATES FROM THE SAME

00:26:28.019 --> 00:26:29.154
PROCESS IT GOES THROUGH. THERE'S

00:26:29.220 --> 00:26:31.823
NO DIFFERENCE CAN DROP OFF FUEL

00:26:31.890 --> 00:26:34.759
IN BLYTHE, CALIFORNIA, AT A GAS

00:26:34.826 --> 00:26:36.594
STATION, AND IT'S OVER $5 A

00:26:36.661 --> 00:26:39.597
GALLON FOR GAS. AS OF

00:26:39.664 --> 00:26:40.699
YESTERDAY'S AVERAGE, THE DAY

